  "mechanismSummary": "The allylic cation is attacked by the nearest alkene of its own chain, which makes a six-membered ring and a new cation; the next alkene catches that one, and the alkyne catches the third, closing a five-membered ring. Three rings and four new stereocentres form in one operation, all trans-fused, because the chain folds into a chair–chair shape and the trans alkenes of the chain fix the relative configuration (the app does not check stereochemistry yet). The alkyne is the terminator: it gives a linear vinyl cation outside the D ring, which ethylene carbonate captures. Work-up turns the adduct into a methyl ketone, so the tetracycle carries the C-17 acetyl group of progesterone. Johnson obtained the tetracyclic diketone in good yield, mainly with the side chain in the natural 17β position (some 17α isomer also forms).",
